   "The look-alikes are dominated by one recent stretch ending 02 Mar 2026, with a smaller contribution from 17 Feb 2025; the rest carry very little weight. In the week after those, cancellations tended to fall. Those look-alikes sit in late winter to early spring and, importantly, follow school-holiday or short-week disruptions back into normal five-day weeks, which is similar to our path out of Easter (two short holiday weeks, then a normal week). For GP reports, the influences that matter most are working days and bank holidays (admin teams\u2019 availability), plus school holidays that disrupt scheduling and rebooking. On those, the look-alikes and the forecast week largely match: 20 Apr 2026 is a full, non-holiday week with schools back. This feels more than a coincidence in the numbers: broadly genuine.",
   "The forecast points to a clear fall on the latest week and a slight fall on the last month and quarter. For a normal five-day week right after Easter, that sounds reasonable: operations usually settle after holiday noise, and the look-alikes mostly point downward. In practice, free cancellations and income at risk should edge below recent levels rather than drop sharply. One thing to watch is any lingering post-Easter rebooking ripple that could push late changes into this week despite the cleaner calendar."
